finding: Help does not consistently override invalid/incomplete argv, and the new help command cannot itself be queried with --help. Independently reproduced on HEAD: `bun bin/shallot.ts help --help` exits 1 with `unknown command: --help`; `bun bin/shallot.ts dev --target --help` and `build --target= --help` exit 1 with `--target requires a platform`; `bun bin/shallot.ts migrate extra --help` exits 1 with `migrate takes no arguments`. This breaks the advertised `shallot <command> --help` contract for help itself and clig.dev's append-help-to-an-incomplete-command guidance. In src/cli/index.ts:138-158 and 173-194, resolve help requests before validating other arguments (while retaining unknown help-subject errors without a help flag), and add direct/parser tests for these cases and -h. The existing help and top-level precedence tests all pass despite this gap. Both requested suites independently pass at each of all six commits; no source edits or pre-land/packed tests were run.
